use std
into fea_mesh.amni
dialect js

This file is a library built for the web as a wasm module; its `main()` does nothing. JavaScript drives it through its exported functions (every name starting with fm_ is exported). It is a port of the hexahedral finite element core of cad/fea_mesh.js: the QM6 solid element with its thin-shell variant, the 8-node heat element, nodal volumes, hanging-node masters, the sparse pattern, assembly and the stress pass. Results are compared bit for bit with the JavaScript, so every floating-point formula keeps the JavaScript evaluation order exactly: arithmetic is f64, each sum starts at 0.0 and adds its terms one at a time in loop order, products and quotients group left to right as written (a·b·c is (a·b)·c and a·b/8 is (a·b)/8), a parenthesised group is computed first, and nothing is fused, reordered or vectorized. Integers from the node table are used as reals in formulas. Arrays filled by clearing and resizing get their exact size; nothing is grown by pushing except where stated.

```amni
extern fn fm_view_f64(id i32, xs real[:]) = "fm_view_f64";
extern fn fm_view_f32(id i32, xs f32[:]) = "fm_view_f32";
extern fn fm_view_i32(id i32, xs i32[:]) = "fm_view_i32";
extern fn fm_view_u8(id i32, xs u8[:]) = "fm_view_u8";
var NN int = 0;
var NE int = 0;
var NH int = 0;
var HK int = 4;
var FL int = 0;
var TINIT int = 0;
var X real[>..];
var E i32[>..];
var CB real[>..];
